{"key":"enterprise/T1027.015","id":"T1027.015","name":"Compression","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1027","tactics":["stealth"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may use compression to obfuscate their payloads or files. Compressed file formats such as ZIP, gzip, 7z, and RAR can compress and archive multiple files together to make it easier and faster to transfer files. In addition to compressing files, adversaries may also compress shellcode directly - for example, in order to store it in a Windows Registry key (i.e., Fileless Storage). In order to further evade detection, adversaries may…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1027/015","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--fbd91bfc-75c2-4f0c-8116-3b4e722906b3","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.726Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0055","name":"File Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0055","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--235b7491-2d2b-4617-9a52-3c0783680f71","page":"telemetry/DC0055/"},{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0059","name":"File Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0059","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--639e87f3-acb6-448a-9645-258f20da4bc5","page":"telemetry/DC0059/"},{"id":"DC0061","name":"File Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0061","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--84572de3-9583-4c73-aabd-06ea88123dd8","page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0281","name":"Detection Strategy for Compressed Payload Creation and Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0281","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--f3d5d1d5-3d80-46b2-be05-f0c438625230","relationship_id":"relationship--432c35d1-b40e-401c-8c75-601a5cf0f86e"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0782","name":"Analytic 0782","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0281#AN0782","guidance":"Monitors for compression tool usage (e.g., 7zip, WinRAR, MakeCab) that follows or precedes file modification, suspicious file types (e.g., .exe, .dll) being compressed, or dropped from self-extracting archives followed by immediate execution.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0281"},{"id":"AN0783","name":"Analytic 0783","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0281#AN0783","guidance":"Detects sequential command-line compression utilities (e.g., gzip, tar, zip, 7z) followed by execution of unpacked files, especially in temp directories or under non-standard locations like /dev/shm or /tmp with ELF binaries.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0281"},{"id":"AN0784","name":"Analytic 0784","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0281#AN0784","guidance":"Identifies archive utilities (e.g., ditto, unzip, xar, pkgutil) used to extract payloads to non-standard paths, then correlates with execution or file permission changes (e.g., `chmod +x`) and process spawns from decompressed location.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0281"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0782","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0281#AN0782","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0039","component":"File Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=11","platforms":["Windows"],